      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name}, I don't have the same level of expertise that OP does, but I recorded a video of the phenomenon.\n\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1153442862101450844/1154904122219315251/2023-09-22_16-57-39.mp4\n\nI have an avatar with a expression that toggles the gameobject with the skinned mesh. It also has a sibling gameobject that is just a tiny, regular unity cube, that is always enabled. When the cube is in view for the client, they see the avatar reappear. When the cube is OUT of view for the client, they DON'T see the avatar reappear until the cube reenters their view, OR the avatar is reset by either of them.\n\nI think that the takeaway is: if a client is culling or disabling all renderers on a remote avatar, animations won't play from the client's perspective. So you can see how an avatar that disables then re-enables all its renderers could cause that avatar to get stuck invisible, from other clients' perspectives.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
